  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Erection of an additional single‑storey rear extension to the existing rear extension, creating a total rear projection of 6 metres. The extension will form a new open‑plan kitchen and dining area. Works include associated internal alterations and external finishes as per previously approved with no changes.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed element, by reason of its excessive size and scale, and siting would result in a development that is overbearing and would cause an unacceptable loss of light on the neighbouring property, contrary to the Residential Extension Guidelines, and Local Plan Policies CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations), and the principles of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed extension, by virtue of its excessive size, bulk, projection, and siting, would fail to appear subordinate to the host property. Furthermore, given the site's prominent corner location, the development would result in an unduly dominant, visually incongruous, and unbalanced form when viewed from the public realm. As such, it would be harmful to the character and appearance of the host dwelling, the adjoining terraced properties, and the wider street scene. The proposal therefore would fail to conserve or enhance the character of the area, contrary to Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations) of the adopted Local Plan."
  ],
